From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rmtfs: fix verbose CLOSE logging argument types

The CLOSE request carries an integer caller ID, not a path. Passing it to
%s can dereference an invalid pointer, and the fourth conversion reads a
missing argument. This happens before sending the CLOSE response when -v
is enabled. Print the caller ID as unsigned and match the three arguments.
Annotate the debug wrapper so the compiler checks its call sites.

Source reviewed: https://github.com/linux-msm/rmtfs/blob/b30a3eb38f9af283f18dbd3c7755653efc52c094/rmtfs.c
This is a local correction, not an imported upstream fix.

--- a/rmtfs.c
+++ b/rmtfs.c
@@ -30,7 +30,8 @@
 static char slot_suffix[SLOT_SUFFIX_LEN];
 
 static bool dbgprintf_enabled;
-static void dbgprintf(const char *fmt, ...)
+static void __attribute__((format(printf, 1, 2)))
+dbgprintf(const char *fmt, ...)
 {
 	va_list ap;
 
@@ -127,7 +128,7 @@
 	rmtfs_mem_free(rmem);
 
 respond:
-	dbgprintf("[RMTFS] close %s => %d (%d:%d)\n",
+	dbgprintf("[RMTFS] close %u => (%d:%d)\n",
 		  req.caller_id, resp.result.result, resp.result.error);
 
 	len = qmi_encode_message(&resp_buf,
